Description: sysinit uses the dependency cache on bare metal
 do_sysinit() forced a rebuild of the dependency tree at every boot, so the
 cache that init.sh restores from $RC_LIBEXECDIR/cache was never used
 there: on a Nokia N950 (OMAP3, 1 GHz) that rebuild of 86 scripts took
 12 s of every boot. The force is there because the system type (LXC,
 Docker, Xen, ...) is only known once /proc is mounted and changes the
 keywords. On bare metal (rc_sys() is NULL) the type cannot change, so the
 tree is rebuilt only when a script or config is newer than the cache, or
 there is no cache, as everywhere else.
Author: Sebastian Matkovich <smatkovi@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no
--- a/src/openrc/rc.c
+++ b/src/openrc/rc.c
@@ -530,8 +530,11 @@ do_sysinit(void)
 	 * sys */
 	if ((sys = rc_sys()))
 		setenv("RC_SYS", sys, 1);
-	/* force an update of the dependency tree */
-	if ((main_deptree = _rc_deptree_load(1, NULL)) == NULL)
+	/* force an update of the dependency tree in a container or VM, whose
+	 * type changes the keywords; on bare metal the cache init.sh restored
+	 * is rebuilt only when a script or config is newer than it, or there
+	 * is none */
+	if ((main_deptree = _rc_deptree_load(sys ? 1 : 0, NULL)) == NULL)
 		eerrorx("failed to load deptree");
 }
 
